    "long_instructions": "Great job giving your fish a starring role with that heading! Now let's tell everyone a little more about your finned friend.\r\n\r\nOpen the `index.html` file. You'll see the `<h1>` tag you added for your fish's name. We want to add some more text right below it.\r\n\r\nBelow the `<h1>` tag, add a new tag: `<p>`. This stands for 'paragraph'. Inside the opening `<p>` and closing `</p>` tags, write a short 1-3 sentence description of your pet fish. You can talk about its color, what it likes to eat, or its personality!\r\n\r\nFor example, you could write: `<p>Finley is a bright orange goldfish with shiny scales. He loves to chase the bubbles from the filter and nibble on his algae wafers. Sometimes, he even tries to race his reflection!</p>`\r\n\r\nWhen you're done, your web page will have a heading and a description for your pet fish!",
    "generate_outline": "Students will add a `<p>` tag below the `<h1>` tag in the `<body>`. The content of the `<p>` tag should be a short 1-3 sentence description of their pet fish, like its color, personality, or what it likes to do."
